item.description:
250-750 CAD | FutureOS — Phase 1: Creation of the FutureOS launch site on Wix Studio

OBJECTIVE

Create an initial professional, bilingual, and functional version of the FutureOS website to:

*   present the project;
*   recruit Founding Partners;
*   recruit representatives and collaborators;
*   collect applications;
*   sell the first authorized programs;
*   launch marketing campaigns;
*   track sign-ups and conversions.

PLATFORM

The site must be built using Wix Studio, primarily utilizing:

*   Wix CMS;
*   Wix Forms;
*   Wix CRM;
*   Wix Automations;
*   Wix Multilingual;
*   Wix Pricing Plans or Wix Stores;
*   Wix Payments, Stripe, or PayPal;
*   Wix SEO;
*   Google Analytics 4;
*   Google Search Console.

Velo by Wix will be used only when a feature cannot be implemented using native tools.

PAGES TO CREATE

1. Home — Home / Global Launch

The page will include:

*   the FutureOS value proposition;
*   problems solved;
*   user profiles;
*   an overview of AI agents;
*   an overview of the Contributor Hub;
*   key benefits;
*   available programs;
*   calls to action;
*   a brief FAQ;
*   newsletter sign-up.

2. How FutureOS Works

Present the user journey:

*   create a profile;
*   present a project or a need;
*   find collaborators and partners;
*   use services and AI agents;
*   participate in missions;
*   build a FutureOS reputation.

3. FutureOS Solutions

Present the main categories:

*   project development;
*   recruitment;
*   collaboration;
*   sales;
*   marketing;
*   automation;
*   funding and partners;
*   project management;
*   professional services;
*   artificial intelligence.

4. Founding Partners

Include:

*   the vision;
*   the role of early partners;
*   participation levels;
*   benefits; * rewards and credits;
* intended use of contributions;
* terms and conditions;
* an FAQ;
* the registration form;
* authorized payment options.

No financial returns, shares, or future value may be promised without a compliant legal structure.

5. Become a Representative

Present:

* the role;
* responsibilities;
* target markets;
* the compensation system;
* advancement opportunities;
* training;
* the application form;
* country and region selection.

6. Join as a Contributor

This page will be aimed at:

* freelancers;
* developers;
* designers;
* AI specialists;
* salespeople;
* recruiters;
* marketing professionals;
* future founding members.

It will present tasks, points, rewards, credits, and the future Contributor Hub.

7. Roadmap and Progress

Create a dynamic page presenting:

* project phases;
* objectives;
* completed items;
* items in development;
* next steps;
* a progress bar;
* recent updates.

Data must be editable via the Wix CMS.

8. Support FutureOS

Present the various ways to support the project:

* join the program;
* become a partner;
* become a representative;
* contribute as a professional;
* offer services or technologies;
* share FutureOS;
* request a strategic partnership.

9. About

Include:

* mission;
* vision;
* project history;
* values;
* international ambition;
* responsible artificial intelligence;
* founder introduction;
* overview of the team being sought.

10. FAQ and Contact

Create:

* an FAQ organized by category;
* a general inquiry form;
* a partnership form;
* a support form;
* contact details;
* language selection;
* request type selection. PHASE 1 FORMS

Create and test:

*   General registration;
*   Founding Partner;
*   Representative;
*   Collaborator;
*   Strategic partner;
*   Information request;
*   Newsletter sign-up.

Each form must:

*   Save the contact in Wix CRM;
*   Automatically add a tag;
*   Identify the page and lead source;
*   Record a referral code if applicable;
*   Send a confirmation;
*   Notify the administrator;
*   Include necessary consents;
*   Be protected against unwanted submissions.

PAYMENTS

Configure the initial FutureOS programs or packages with:

*   Price;
*   Currency;
*   Description;
*   Taxes;
*   Payment;
*   Confirmation;
*   Invoice;
*   Refund policy;
*   Terms and conditions;
*   Promo codes.

Specific copy and products will be provided or approved by FutureOS prior to launch.

BASIC AUTOMATIONS

Configure:

1.  Welcome email.
2.  Confirmation for each form.
3.  Administrative notification.
4.  Payment confirmation.
5.  Automatic tagging in Wix CRM.
6.  Follow-up for interested leads.
7.  Founding Partner sequence.
8.  Representative sequence.
9.  Collaborator sequence.
10. Addition to appropriate newsletter lists.

BILINGUAL VERSION
